Let $k\geq0$ and $b\geq1$ be integers, let $H$ be a CNF of width at most $k$ on $[d]$, and let $0<p<1$. Choose $T\subseteq[d]$ by retaining each coordinate independently with probability $p$, and choose a uniform assignment $\rho$ outside $T$. Suppose $$\label{eq:restriction-theta}
  \theta=\sum_{\ell=b+1}^{k}\binom{k}{\ell}
                  \left(\frac{2p}{1-p}\right)^{\ell}<1.$$ There are numbers $W(H,T,\rho)\geq 0$, depending only on the formula and the restriction, such that $$\label{eq:restriction-cost}
  \mathbb E_{T,\rho}W(H,T,\rho)\leq\frac{1}{1-\theta}$$ and, simultaneously for every real-valued function $G$ on $\{0,1\}^T$, $$\label{eq:restriction-correlation}
  \left|\mathbb E_z G(z)H_{T,\rho}(z)\right|
       \leq W(H,T,\rho)\,\mathop{\mathrm{corr}}_b(G).$$ An empty sum in <a href="#eq:restriction-theta" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:restriction-theta">[eq:restriction-theta]</a> is zero.

For an input of length $n$, put $d=\left\lfloor n/5\right\rfloor$ and reject if $d<64$. Otherwise define $$r=\left\lceil d^{2/3}\right\rceil,\qquad
 t=\max\{j\in\mathbb N\cup\{0\}: j\text{ is even and }j^6\le d\}.$$ Reject if fewer than $2d+(t+2)r-1$ input bits are available. Otherwise parse the input into the following consecutive blocks:

1.  $d$ data bits $x=(x_1,\ldots,x_d)$;

2.  $d+r-1$ hash bits $u_1,\ldots,u_{d+r-1}$;

3.  $r$ bits $p_0,\ldots,p_{r-1}$, encoding the monic polynomial $$P(Z)=Z^r+\sum_{i=0}^{r-1}p_iZ^i\in\mathbb F_2[Z];$$

4.  $t$ blocks of $r$ bits, encoding elements $\beta_0,\ldots,\beta_{t-1}$ of the quotient ring $R_P=\mathbb F_2[Z]/(P)$, in the basis represented by $1,Z,\ldots,Z^{r-1}$.



Unused bits are ignored. Form $$\label{eq:toeplitz-hash}
 h_i(x)=\sum_{s=1}^d u_{i+s-1}x_s\pmod2
 \quad(1\le i\le r),\qquad
 h(x)=\sum_{i=1}^r h_i(x)Z^{i-1}\in R_P.$$ Let $\lambda:R_P\to\mathbb F_2$ take the degree-zero coefficient of the unique representative of degree less than $r$. The input belongs to $L$ exactly when $$\label{eq:language-evaluation}
 \lambda\left(\sum_{j=0}^{t-1}\beta_jh(x)^j\right)=0.$$
